$text2speech — Kokoro TTS (text → sounds[])



SUMMARY

  Synthesizes speech from texts[] and/or prompts[] using Kokoro-82M (hexgrad/kokoro).
  Default backend: pip kokoro + KPipeline. Optional legacy: HF clone in models/kokoro/
  with models.py + kokoro.generate (user prototype style).



SYNTAX

  $text2speech
  $text2speech(voice=af_bella, speed=1.0)
  $text2speech(voice=@voices)   — one WAV per voice from @voices texts[] ($list)
  $text2speech(voice=models/kokoro/voices/af_bella.pt)



INPUT

  texts[] and/or prompts[] — at least one non-empty string.



OUTPUT

  sounds[] — one 24 kHz WAV per input text per voice ({timestamp}_{index}_{voice}.wav).



ARGUMENTS

  voice= — Kokoro voice id (default af_bella) or voice=@ref for several.

  device= — cuda, cpu, or auto (pipeline backend).

  speed= — speech rate (default 1.0).

  split= — sentence | paragraph | newline | none (pipeline chunking).

  chunk_by= — legacy backend only; sentence splits on "." like the prototype.

  repo_id= — HuggingFace repo id (default hexgrad/Kokoro-82M); files go to models/kokoro/.

  espeak_lib= — path to libespeak-ng.dll (Windows) for G2P fallback.



MODELS

  models/kokoro/config.json
  models/kokoro/kokoro-v1_0.pth   (or kokoro-v0_19.pth for legacy)
  models/kokoro/voices/af_bella.pt

  Missing files are downloaded on first use directly into models/kokoro/ (not ~/.cache/huggingface).
  Legacy backend: clone https://huggingface.co/hexgrad/Kokoro-82M into models/kokoro instead.



REQUIREMENTS

  kokoro + espeak-ng + spaCy en_core_web_sm in .venvs/text2speech.
  Setup: powershell -File tools\setup_external_venvs.ps1
  Windows: place libespeak-ng.dll in tools\libespeak-ng.dll (default), or install eSpeak NG.



ENVIRONMENT

  AH_EMULATE_TEXT2SPEECH=1 — stub files without kokoro.
  AH_TEXT2SPEECH_BACKEND=pipeline | legacy — force backend (default: legacy if models.py exists).
  AH_KOKORO_DIR= — model/voice root (default models/kokoro).
  AH_KOKORO_MODEL= — checkpoint path for legacy backend.
  AH_ESPEAK_LIBRARY= — espeak-ng DLL/.so path.



EXAMPLE

  @script: $file(path=story.txt) -> $only(texts)
  @say: @script -> $text2speech(voice=bm_george)



PROMPT-CONSUMING

  No (texts/prompts pass through unless downstream steps clear them).
